  partName: Intake Manifold Stud
  description: The Intake Manifold Stud is a tiny, elongated component located at
    the top-center-front of the engine, made of Material.001, and is responsible
    for fastening the intake manifold to the engine block. Its primary function is
    to maintain a secure seal and ensure proper airflow into the engine, and its
    material composition provides the necessary strength and durability. Notably,
    the Intake Manifold Stud is designed to withstand the mechanical stresses and
    thermal fluctuations associated with engine operation, making it a critical component
    for optimal engine performance.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
